WasmFS: keep a NUL byte written to stdout or stderr

The standard streams buffered output a line at a time and ended a line
on a NUL byte as well as on a line break, since each line went to
emscripten_out() or emscripten_err() as a C string; flush() wrote a NUL
to push out the last line. So a NUL byte came out as a line break, and
"a\0b\n" printed "a\nb\n". End lines only on a line break, hand each one
to out() or err() with its length, NUL bytes included, and have flush()
write the buffered line directly.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-stdout-nul.md

